# AutoCAD lock and autosave files — regenerated every session, never content
*.dwl
*.dwl2
*.sv$
*.ac$
*.err

# ⚠️ FIXED 10/08/2026. This block used to end with a bare `*.log`, and it was silently excluding
# 18 LESSON BUILD LOGS under projects/שיעור-*/files/ — full_build.log, live_run.log,
# R2-truth-test.log, build_bolts/members/plates.log. Those are the record of what was actually
# built in each lesson, not session noise; the comment above says "never content" and it was
# wrong about them. AutoCAD's own logs are named, so name them:
acad*.log
*.err.log
plot.log
# and nothing else — a lesson log is content.

# AutoCAD's own rolling .bak of the previous save — automatic and redundant, never kept.
# (The *-backup-*.dwg snapshots are deliberate LOCAL evidence: they sit next to the model
#  until archived into sandbox/_archive/ — see the rule near the end — and stay out of the
#  repo either way. Corrected 12/08/2026: this note used to say they ARE kept in the repo.)
*.bak

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# the plugin's scratch I/O files — written and overwritten on every single op
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_cmd.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_result.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_expect_dwg.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_holes.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_list.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_posnum.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_posauto.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_groupauto.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_conndump.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_basedump.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_purlin.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_cat.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_sections.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_styles.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_enums.txt
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_catalog.txt

# --- added 09/08/2026, development-folder tidy ---
# Compiled plugin binaries: rebuildable from the .cs beside them, and 125 of them were
# most of a 54 MB .git. The SOURCES stay tracked — they are the written history of the API.
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/*.dll
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/*.pdb

# Transient op output. Every one of these is written by an op and read straight back;
# they regenerate on demand and carry no history.
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/eb_*.txt
# ⭐ 17/08/2026: the three exceptions that used to sit here (eb_cmd / eb_result /
# eb_expect_dwg) are gone. They were tracked as "the last live state", and that stopped
# being true: the command file is now CONSUMED as it is read, the result is written per
# model into ch/<slot>/, and the pin is a mirror of data/worksession.json. Tracking them
# only produced a file that flickers in and out of every commit.

# --- added 17/08/2026, the per-model mailboxes and the work-session registry ---
# One channel folder per open drawing (v185): the same transient command/result/output
# files as above, only sorted by model instead of shared. Machine state, never content.
api+knowledge-develop/app/plugin/ch/
# WHO is working on WHAT right now, with timestamps and owners. It describes this machine
# at this moment; the PROCEDURE is what belongs in the repo (findings/PARALLEL-MODELS.md).
api+knowledge-develop/data/worksession.json

# Archived DWG snapshots — kept on disk, out of the repo
api+knowledge-develop/projects/sandbox/_archive/

# eb_api.save()'s timestamped snapshots land next to the model and are moved to _archive/
# when a part closes; until then they are deliberate local backups, not repo content.
api+knowledge-develop/projects/sandbox/*-backup-*.dwg
